its actually mostly the same as the one before. it is still using ImageManager.loadXxx to create a bitmap and creates a new sprite out of it, but its been split into 2 lines, uses loadPicture instead of loadBHud, and has a different actor reference. if you aim to use loadPicture, the game is going to be looking for a file in the pictures folder named... something. otherwise, you could try using the same bhud files with the bhud function. The reference to the actor within the BattleResults looks to be this._actor instead of this._battler.
using the same convention, try
Code:
//==============================
// * Create Actor Sprite
//==============================
