And the last think I should bring up is the error message that pops up whenever I try to use the modified version of the plugin I've been trying to get working.
Code:
$gameTemp._ougiData[1]._actorId is not a function
Part of me believes that the issue could be the fact that there needs to be an addition to the whole "ougiData[number]" parts of the script, comparing the code used in this plugin to the other modified plugins shows that they're something of an outlier here, though I may be mistaken and the issue might have more to do with something else entirely.
I feel like it's also worth mentioning that the script was also slightly modified prior to this, just to change file names for the images used for the primary PNG used in front of the backdrop to be "ActorOugi_id" as opposed to just simply being the same "Actor_id" image that the victory screen would pull from. And that's not mentioning the background images which while I left the file names the same for them during my initial edit, they are still roughly similar to the change I made to the primary images I had been using, being "Actor_id_Ougi". I feel that it was different enough to not bring up any issues, however perhaps something went over my head in the process.
